message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Kaleidohedra: the Euclid–Kepler cell and the Euclid–Kepler network"
authors:
  - name: "DICTO"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DICTOR-Master/kaleidohedra"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
keywords:
  - "Euclid–Kepler cell"
  - "Euclid–Kepler network"
  - "great stellated dodecahedron"
  - "icosahedron"
  - "dodecahedron"
  - "golden ratio"
abstract: >-
  Euclid's roofs on a cube make the regular dodecahedron; folding the roof
  vertices back through the cube faces makes the regular icosahedron, edges
  φ² : φ : 1, each roof vertex landing on a neighbouring cell's icosahedron.
  On a simple cubic lattice: 13 nodes per cell, Pm-3, with every cell's 31
  icosahedral axes aligned. Great stellated dodecahedra on the even cells and
  icosahedra on the odd cells share only corners (the Euclid–Kepler network).
  Every claim is checked by scripts/verify-roof-fold.mjs. See DISCOVERIES.md #8.
